{
  "meta": {
    "version": 1,
    "last_updated": "2026-04-12",
    "title": "SprintView: Dependencies blank for Sprint 2 & 3 due to schema field mismatch",
    "owner": "vibe-qa-general"
  },
  "quick_facts": {
    "bug_id": "BUG-0001",
    "severity": "medium",
    "status": "fixed",
    "sprint": "1"
  },
  "content": {
    "tldr": "SprintView was only reading content.dependencies to populate the 'Dependencies' section. Sprint 2 and Sprint 3 JSON files use content.prerequisites instead, causing that section to render blank for those sprints.",
    "environment": "wiki-app (Next.js) — sprint detail view for any sprint using 'prerequisites' key",
    "steps_to_reproduce": [
      "Open the wiki-app in a browser.",
      "Navigate to Plan → Sprint 2 (or Sprint 3).",
      "Observe that the 'Dependencies' section is absent / empty.",
      "Inspect wiki/plan/sprints/sprint-2.json and confirm the field is 'prerequisites', not 'dependencies'."
    ],
    "expected_behavior": "The 'Dependencies' section should list all prerequisite/dependency items for every sprint, regardless of which field name the JSON file uses.",
    "actual_behavior": "The 'Dependencies' section was hidden for Sprint 2 and Sprint 3 because SprintView only read content.dependencies; sprint-2.json and sprint-3.json use content.prerequisites.",
    "root_cause": "Schema inconsistency: sprint-1.json uses 'dependencies' while sprint-2.json and sprint-3.json use 'prerequisites'. SprintView only merged the former, so the latter was silently ignored.",
    "fix_description": "Updated SprintView in wiki-app/components/views/PlanView.tsx to merge both fields:\n  const dependencies = [\n    ...((content.dependencies as string[] | undefined) ?? []),\n    ...((content.prerequisites as string[] | undefined) ?? []),\n  ];\nThis is a backwards-compatible read; all sprint JSON files continue to work unchanged."
  },
  "audit": [
    {
      "version": 1,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T00:00:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-qa-general",
      "action": "created",
      "note": "Bug identified: SprintView only read content.dependencies; sprint-2 and sprint-3 use content.prerequisites."
    },
    {
      "version": 2,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T00:01:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-backend-general",
      "action": "fixed",
      "note": "SprintView updated to spread both content.dependencies and content.prerequisites into a single array before rendering."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "meta": {
    "version": 1,
    "last_updated": "2026-04-12",
    "title": "ImpactMap section index crashes with React error #31 for relation files with goal-as-object",
    "owner": "vibe-qa-general"
  },
  "quick_facts": {
    "bug_id": "BUG-0002",
    "severity": "high",
    "status": "fixed",
    "sprint": "1"
  },
  "content": {
    "tldr": "Navigating to /wiki/impact-map throws React error #31 ('Objects are not valid as a React child') because the section index preview loader used d.goal directly as a string — but invoice-relations, order-relations, and product-relations store goal as { statement, metric, deadline }.",
    "environment": "wiki-app (Next.js) — /wiki/impact-map section index page",
    "steps_to_reproduce": [
      "Open the wiki-app in a browser.",
      "Click Impact Map in the sidebar (or navigate to /wiki/impact-map).",
      "Observe a blank page and the following console error: 'Error: Minified React error #31; object with keys {statement, metric, deadline}'"
    ],
    "expected_behavior": "The impact-map section index should list all relation files as preview cards, showing the goal statement as a readable string excerpt.",
    "actual_behavior": "The page crashes with React error #31 because the preview loader set tldr = d.goal (an object), which React cannot render as a child node.",
    "root_cause": "In wiki-app/app/wiki/[section]/page.tsx, the loadPreview() function had: `(d.goal as string | undefined)`. TypeScript cast does not convert the value at runtime — for files that use goal: { statement, metric, deadline }, the object was silently passed through and then rendered verbatim in JSX, triggering error #31.",
    "fix_description": "Updated loadPreview() in [section]/page.tsx to detect when d.goal is an object and extract .statement:\n  const rawGoal = d.goal;\n  const goalString =\n    rawGoal !== null && typeof rawGoal === 'object' && !Array.isArray(rawGoal)\n      ? ((rawGoal as Record<string, unknown>).statement as string | undefined)\n      : (rawGoal as string | undefined);\nAlso created wiki-app/components/views/BugView.tsx for a readable, styled bug-report page (previously rendered as raw JSON)."
  },
  "audit": [
    {
      "version": 1,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T06:00:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-qa-general",
      "action": "created",
      "note": "Bug identified: section index page crashes on impact-map because goal object is passed directly into JSX."
    },
    {
      "version": 2,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T06:05:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-frontend-general",
      "action": "fixed",
      "note": "Fixed loadPreview() to unpack goal object; created BugView.tsx for readable bug pages."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "meta": {
    "version": 1,
    "last_updated": "2026-04-12",
    "title": "Login succeeds but user is immediately redirected back to /login — TransformInterceptor envelope not unwrapped on frontend",
    "owner": "vibe-qa-general"
  },
  "quick_facts": {
    "bug_id": "BUG-0003",
    "severity": "critical",
    "status": "fixed",
    "sprint": "2"
  },
  "content": {
    "tldr": "Admin could authenticate successfully (POST /auth/login returned 200) but was sent back to /login immediately. The accessToken was never stored in Zustand because the frontend read data.accessToken from the raw axios response, while the backend TransformInterceptor wraps every response as { data: <payload>, meta: { timestamp } }.",
    "environment": "frontend (React + Zustand) — all auth + product API calls. Reproducible with any role including admin.",
    "steps_to_reproduce": [
      "Navigate to http://localhost/ (redirects to /login).",
      "Enter valid admin credentials (e.g. admin@store.vn).",
      "Submit the login form.",
      "Observe: the page navigates to /products then immediately bounces back to /login.",
      "Open DevTools → Application → Local Storage → 'eam-auth': confirm accessToken is null."
    ],
    "expected_behavior": "After successful login, accessToken and refreshToken are stored in Zustand (persisted to localStorage), and the user stays on /products.",
    "actual_behavior": "POST /auth/login returns HTTP 200 with body { data: { accessToken, refreshToken, user }, meta: { timestamp } }. The frontend did apiClient.post<LoginResponse>('/auth/login'), then read data.accessToken — but axios data here is the full envelope { data: {...}, meta: {...} }, so data.accessToken is undefined. setTokens(undefined, undefined) is called; RequireAuth sees null accessToken and redirects to /login.",
    "root_cause": "The global NestJS TransformInterceptor (backend/src/common/interceptors/transform.interceptor.ts) wraps every response payload. The frontend api-client.ts had NO envelope-unwrapping logic, so every apiClient call received the envelope as the payload. This silently broke login (and would have broken all product API calls too once auth was working).",
    "fix_description": "Added a response interceptor in frontend/src/lib/api-client.ts that checks for the { data, meta } envelope and unwraps it before any caller sees the response:\n\n  apiClient.interceptors.response.use((res) => {\n    if (res.data && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(res.data, 'data')) {\n      res.data = res.data.data;\n    }\n    return res;\n  }, ...);\n\nAlso fixed the raw axios.post in the refresh-token path (which bypasses apiClient interceptors) to manually unwrap: reads envelope.data instead of data directly.",
    "affected_files": [
      "frontend/src/lib/api-client.ts"
    ],
    "regression_risk": "Low. The unwrap guard uses hasOwnProperty('data') — only envelopes match. Any non-envelope response (e.g. 204 No Content) passes through unchanged."
  },
  "audit": [
    {
      "version": 1,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T12:00:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-qa-general",
      "action": "created",
      "note": "Bug reported by user: logged in as admin, cannot access /products. Root cause identified: TransformInterceptor envelope not unwrapped."
    },
    {
      "version": 2,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T12:05:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-frontend-general",
      "action": "fixed",
      "note": "Added response interceptor to api-client.ts to unwrap { data, meta } envelope. Fixed refresh-token raw axios path separately. Branch: fix/BUG-0003-api-envelope-unwrap."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "meta": {
    "version": 1,
    "last_updated": "2026-04-12",
    "title": "Admin user storeId null coerced to empty string in JWT strategy causes UUID crash in all products endpoints",
    "owner": "vibe-qa-general"
  },
  "quick_facts": {
    "bug_id": "BUG-0004",
    "severity": "critical",
    "status": "fixed",
    "sprint": "2"
  },
  "content": {
    "tldr": "Admin user has store_id = NULL in the database. JwtStrategy converted null to '' (empty string) via `?? ''`. Any products API call then passed '' as a UUID to PostgreSQL, crashing with: QueryFailedError: invalid input syntax for type uuid: \"\".",
    "environment": "backend (NestJS) — all products endpoints (POST /products, GET /products, GET /products/:id, PATCH /products/:id, PATCH /products/:id/deactivate). Reproducible by calling any products endpoint while authenticated as admin.",
    "steps_to_reproduce": [
      "Login as admin@eam.local (store_id is NULL in DB).",
      "Call GET /api/v1/products with a valid Bearer token.",
      "Observe: 500 Internal Server Error — QueryFailedError: invalid input syntax for type uuid: \"\""
    ],
    "expected_behavior": "Admin users without a store assignment receive HTTP 403 Forbidden with message 'Store assignment required to list products' instead of a 500 crash.",
    "actual_behavior": "JwtStrategy.validate() returned storeId: '' (empty string) for admin. ProductsService.findAll() passed '' directly to TypeORM WHERE clause. PostgreSQL attempted to cast '' to UUID and threw a fatal query error, resulting in an unhandled 500.",
    "root_cause": "backend/src/modules/auth/strategies/jwt.strategy.ts line 40: `storeId: user.storeId ?? ''` coerces null to empty string. The empty string is an invalid UUID. ProductsService and StoresService had no null guard before passing storeId to repository queries.",
    "fix_description": "Three-file fix:\n1. current-user.decorator.ts — widened AuthUser.storeId type from `string` to `string | null`.\n2. jwt.strategy.ts — removed `?? ''` fallback; storeId is now passed as-is (null preserved).\n3. products.service.ts — added ForbiddenException guard at top of every public method (create, findAll, findOne, update, deactivate) before any DB query.\n4. stores.service.ts — widened findMyStore(storeId) to accept `string | null`; throws ForbiddenException when null.",
    "affected_files": [
      "backend/src/common/decorators/current-user.decorator.ts",
      "backend/src/modules/auth/strategies/jwt.strategy.ts",
      "backend/src/modules/products/products.service.ts",
      "backend/src/modules/stores/stores.service.ts"
    ],
    "regression_risk": "Low. The null guard is a pre-DB early-exit. All existing store-assigned users are unaffected (storeId is always a valid UUID for them)."
  },
  "audit": [
    {
      "version": 1,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T20:30:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-qa-general",
      "action": "created",
      "note": "Bug surfaced during Sprint 2 testing: admin login succeeds but any products API call returns 500. Root cause: null storeId coerced to '' in jwt.strategy.ts."
    },
    {
      "version": 2,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T20:45:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-backend-nestjs",
      "action": "fixed",
      "note": "Preserved null in JWT strategy, widened AuthUser type, added ForbiddenException guards in products and stores services. tsc --noEmit passes clean. Branch: fix/BUG-0004-admin-storeid-null-uuid-crash."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "meta": {
    "version": 1,
    "last_updated": "2026-04-12",
    "title": "eam_backend crashes at startup — @nestjs/event-emitter missing from Docker anonymous node_modules volume",
    "owner": "vibe-qa-general"
  },
  "quick_facts": {
    "bug_id": "BUG-0005",
    "severity": "critical",
    "status": "fixed",
    "sprint": "3"
  },
  "content": {
    "tldr": "After Sprint 3 deployment, eam_backend failed to compile with 4 TS2307 errors for '@nestjs/event-emitter'. The package is in package.json and was correctly installed on the host, but Docker re-used a stale anonymous volume for /app/node_modules that was created before the package was added.",
    "environment": "eam_backend container (Docker development target). Reproducible on any machine that ran 'docker compose up -d --build' without renewing anonymous volumes after a new npm package was added.",
    "steps_to_reproduce": [
      "Install @nestjs/event-emitter on the host: cd backend && npm install @nestjs/event-emitter --save",
      "Run: docker compose up -d --build   (normal rebuild — does NOT renew anon volumes)",
      "Check: docker logs eam_backend",
      "Observe 4 TS2307 errors: Cannot find module '@nestjs/event-emitter'"
    ],
    "expected_behavior": "NestJS compiles cleanly and all order/invoice routes are mapped. @nestjs/event-emitter is resolvable because npm ci installed it during the image build.",
    "actual_behavior": "TypeScript compilation fails with TS2307 in: app.module.ts, invoices.service.ts, orders.service.spec.ts, orders.service.ts. NestJS never starts.",
    "root_cause": "docker-compose.yml defines an anonymous volume '- /app/node_modules' on the backend service. This volume is created on first container start and populated from the image layer. On subsequent 'docker compose up --build' the image IS rebuilt with the new package.json, but Docker REUSES the existing anonymous volume. The bind-mount '- ./backend:/app' overlays the host source, and the stale anonymous volume shadows /app/node_modules — missing @nestjs/event-emitter entirely.",
    "fix_description": "Recreate the backend container forcing Docker to discard the stale anonymous volume:\n\n  docker compose up -d --build --force-recreate --renew-anon-volumes backend\n\nThis creates a fresh /app/node_modules from the rebuillt image layer (npm ci was run against the updated package.json). NestJS started cleanly; all 10 Sprint 3 routes registered.",
    "affected_files": [
      "backend/package.json",
      "docker-compose.yml"
    ],
    "prevention": "After adding new npm packages to a project using Docker Compose with anonymous node_modules volumes, always use '--renew-anon-volumes' on the next 'docker compose up'. The migrate.ps1 script already handles this pattern for the migrate service.",
    "linked_features": [
      "order",
      "invoice"
    ]
  },
  "audit": [
    {
      "version": 1,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T14:23:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-qa-general",
      "action": "created",
      "note": "Bug discovered when eam_backend container failed to start after Sprint 3 deployment. 4 TS2307 errors for @nestjs/event-emitter."
    },
    {
      "version": 2,
      "timestamp": "2026-04-12T14:25:00Z",
      "author": "vibe-devops-docker",
      "action": "fixed",
      "note": "Ran: docker compose up -d --build --force-recreate --renew-anon-volumes backend. Container started; Nest application successfully started confirmed in logs."
    }
  ]
}

